# Security-sensitive paths, gated for when this repo turns on branch
# protection. See CONTRIBUTING.md's "Security & trust" section: cloning
# this repo auto-runs the tracked .claude/settings.json hooks, and
# install.sh symlinks bin/ onto PATH with launchd pointing straight into
# the checkout — a branch here is effectively code that will run
# unattended on someone's machine, not just a diff to read. Everything
# below requires review before it can merge once protection is on;
# unlisted paths still get reviewed by convention, they just aren't
# enforced yet.

/.claude/            @tristankenney
/bin/                 @tristankenney
/install.sh           @tristankenney
/zdevd/launchd/       @tristankenney
/.github/             @tristankenney

# Test fixtures: golden/recorded data a reviewer can't diff by reading
# it (captured session transcripts, tmux control-mode traces, notify
# payloads) — a poisoned fixture is a quiet way to smuggle behavior
# through a test that "still passes".
**/testdata/          @tristankenney
**/*.fixture.json     @tristankenney
